[h1]Basement Building[/h1]
Workshop ID: 3806513504
Mod ID: aparosa_BasementDig
[quote=⚠ Please read before using]
[b]⚠ Single player only for now. Multiplayer support is in development. Do not use on a server.[/b]
[b]⚠ EXPERIMENTAL — please back up your save before trying it.[/b]
I will not answer questions about compatibility with other mods. Please test it yourself.
[/quote]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/daimou1028/pz-basement-building-assets/main/long-en.jpg[/img]

[h2]What this mod does[/h2]
Dig a basement under your base with a shovel. Unlike other basement mods, the basement is registered with the game as a real room:
[list]
[*][b]Counts as indoors[/b] — the game treats the basement as an indoor room, not as open ground.
[*][b]Powered[/b] — while the power grid is on, the basement has grid power and its light switch works.
[*][b]Expandable[/b] — dig one tile at a time past any basement wall. Touching another basement from this mod joins them into one room.
[*][b][NEW] Expand map basements[/b]: dig past the wall of a basement already on the map, too (see "Expansion" below).
[*][b][NEW] Adopt floors from other mods[/b]: right-click a floor another mod placed next to your basement before this update to adopt it into the basement and make it indoors (see "Adopt" below).
[*][b][NEW] Half materials[/b]: Carpenters know half-material Basement and Basement Expansion from the start. Sandbox picks which of 6 professions do (Carpenter, Construction Worker, Lumberjack, Engineer, Repairman, Metalworker; default: Carpenter only). Others learn them from "Magazine: Basement Builder's Guide", found only in containers not opened yet.
[*][b][NEW] Sandbox options[/b]: deepest level (default 0 = no limit, max B32); material amount (x0.25–x3, default x1, applies to all its recipes, not tools); map basement expansion (default on); look when expanding a map basement (default: this mod's wood; option: copy the nearby map basement's walls and floor); adopting other mods' floors (default on); spawn the magazine (default on) and its spawn rate (5 levels, default normal); which of 6 professions get half materials (default: Carpenter). These defaults are also used in non-sandbox modes such as Apocalypse.
[/list]

[h2]Where to find it[/h2]
Click the [b]Building[/b] button on the left side of the screen. All items are in the [b]Carpentry[/b] category, or type "Basement" in the search box. Pick an item, press Build, then place it with the mouse. Press [b]R[/b] to rotate.

