[h2]Rules[/h2]
[h3]Basement (4x2 room with stairs, one level down)[/h3]
[list]
[*]Build it on ground level, or [b][NEW] on a basement floor (no stairs in the 4x2 area) to dig one more level down, as deep as B32[/b]. Press R to choose one of 4 directions.
[*]The area must be loaded and free of trees, walls, solid objects and vehicles.
[*]Where the stairs go down, pick up items lying on the ground first. Floors that are not dirt or grass (for example inside a house) need a crowbar to pry up (not tested much).
[*]The exit square at the top of the stairs (shown in blue) must be walkable.
[*]There must be no basement or man-made objects below.
[*]The light is off when it is built. Use the switch to turn it on.
[/list]
[h3]Basement Expansion (adds one tile)[/h3]
[list]
[*]Point at the tile behind a basement wall.
[*]Walls next to the stairs cannot be expanded.
[*]Touching another basement from this mod joins them into one room.
[*][b][NEW] Basements already on the map can be expanded too (wood wall only). The wall disappears and you can walk through, but it stays a separate room from the map's room.[/b]
[*]A new basement cannot be dug within 1 tile of another room, so there are at least 2 tiles between it and a map basement. Expand the tiles in between to connect them.
[*]Items that were hanging on the removed wall (pictures, switches, etc.) stay, same as the vanilla sledgehammer. To remove them, smash them individually with a sledgehammer (press R to switch target).
[*]Expanded tiles have no light switch.
[*]Wood Wall: the wall look follows your Carpentry level (2–3: level 1 wall, 4–5: level 2, 6+: level 3).
[*]Log Wall: only for log basements. A wooden basement cannot get log walls.
[/list]
[h3]Upgrade Basement Wall[/h3]
[list]
[*]Point at one basement wall (press R to switch between the west and north side of a tile).
[*]Upgrade only: log → level 1 → level 2 → level 3. The wall becomes the level that matches your Carpentry skill.
[*]A corner piece covers two sides and is upgraded as a whole.
[/list]
[h3][NEW] Adopt (floors placed by other mods)[/h3]
[b]This only applies to floor tiles that other mods (such as Building Craft) placed outside a basement wall before this update — new ones can no longer be placed there (see "Other" below).[/b]
[list]
[*]Right-click a floor tile next to your basement and choose [b]"Add this floor to the basement"[/b] to make that tile part of the basement room (indoors).
[*]No materials are needed, and no wall is added automatically.
[*]Floors next to a basement already on the map can be adopted too. This option does not appear on tiles already part of a room, or on floors not next to a basement.
[*]Touching another basement from this mod joins them into one room.
[/list]
[h3]Other[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Vanilla building cannot disassemble basement walls. But if another mod placed a floor outside the wall before this update, you can smash it from the outside with a sledgehammer.[/b]
[*]Vanilla floors can be placed inside the basement, the same as on the ground floor.
[*]Underground, nothing (vanilla or other mods such as Building Craft / Place Anywhere) can be placed outside a room; wall items can still hang on the inner side.
[/list]

[h2]Tested[/h2]
Project Zomboid 42.20.4, single player, macOS. Building from the menu, material use, indoor registration, grid power and the light, walking the stairs, expansion, joining two basements, wall upgrade, save/reload, adopting another mod's floor, and expanding a map basement (both including after reload), and digging down to B18.

[h2]⚠ Not tested / known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Generators: not tested. Only grid power has been checked.
[*]Whether zombies can spawn directly inside a basement: not confirmed (walking down the stairs is normal vanilla game behavior).
[*]If you remove this mod from a save, the basements stay (indoors, with power), but the magazine and the half-material recipes disappear.
[*]After expanding to the north/west or joining two basements, the old room data stays until you reload the save.
[*][b]Digging deeper: parts of the new level can look black. Reload the save, or walk far away and come back, to fix it.[/b]
[/list]
Please report problems in the comments with your game version and any errors from console.txt.
